# Add project specific R8 rules here.
# AGP will combine all keep rule files in src/main/keepRules to pass to R8
#
# For more details, see
#   https://d.android.com/r/tools/r8/keep-rules
#
# This file has no active rules, which is a decision rather than an oversight. R8 is enabled for
# release builds (isMinifyEnabled, isShrinkResources) with no custom rules, so anything that
# genuinely needs keeping should be written here *before* it breaks a release, not after.
#
# Why nothing needs one as of the first public release:
#   - No Class.forName, getDeclaredMethod/getDeclaredField or newInstance in app code.
#   - The only ::class.java uses are ViewModelProvider.Factory `isAssignableFrom` checks and
#     Room.databaseBuilder(..., XDatabase::class.java, ...), all direct constant references.
#   - No serialization library (kotlinx.serialization, Gson, Jackson) and no @Parcelize.
#   - Room's generated _Impl classes are covered by room-runtime's own consumer rules
#     (`-keep class * extends androidx.room.RoomDatabase`); its type converters are constructed
#     directly rather than reflectively.
#   - reorderable ships an empty proguard.txt and does no reflection.
#
# Re-check this list when adding a dependency, not only when adding your own code.

# If your project uses WebView with JS, uncomment the following
# and specify the fully qualified class name to the JavaScript interface
# class:
#-keepclassmembers class fqcn.of.javascript.interface.for.webview {
#   public *;
#}